<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Lumen — what the data says</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fafaf8; --ink: #1a1a1a; --muted: #6b7280;
    --accent: #0f766e; --warn: #b45309; --line: #e5e7eb;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }
  body { font: 18px/1.55 "Inter", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; }
  .slide {
    min-height: 100vh; padding: 80px 10vw; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .slide.title { background: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); }
  .slide.title h1 { font-size: 56px; line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 16px; font-weight: 700; }
  .slide.title p { color: #d1d5db; font-size: 22px; margin: 0; }
  .slide h2 { font-size: 36px; margin: 0 0 24px; font-weight: 600; }
  .slide h3 { font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 12px; color: var(--accent); }
  .slide p, .slide li { font-size: 20px; max-width: 70ch; }
  .lede { font-size: 28px; line-height: 1.4; font-weight: 500; max-width: 30ch; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .kpis { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 32px; margin: 32px 0; }
  .kpi { padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: white; }
  .kpi .n { font-size: 48px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }
  .kpi .label { color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 48px; align-items: start; }
  blockquote { font-size: 28px; line-height: 1.4; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
               padding-left: 24px; color: var(--ink); font-style: italic; margin: 24px 0; }
  .chart { background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px;
           font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; white-space: pre; color: var(--muted); }
  .pill { display: inline-block; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: white;
          border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  nav.toc { position: fixed; top: 24px; right: 24px; }
  nav.toc a { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%;
              background: var(--line); margin-left: 6px; }
  table.summary { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 24px; }
  table.summary td, table.summary th { padding: 10px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
                                       text-align: left; font-size: 18px; }
  table.summary th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }
  .ask { font-size: 32px; font-weight: 600; }
  .footnote { position: absolute; bottom: 24px; right: 10vw; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  @media print {
    .slide { min-height: 0; page-break-after: always; padding: 60px; }
    nav.toc { display: none; }
  }

  .delta.up { color: var(--accent); }
  .delta.down { color: var(--warn); }
  .note { border-left: 3px solid var(--line); padding-left: 16px; color: var(--muted);
          font-size: 16px; margin-top: 24px; }
  .source { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<section class="slide title">
  <h1>What the data is telling us<br>about Lumen.</h1>
  <p>A story in seven charts. No SQL required.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:48px; font-size:16px;">
    {{ window_label }} · generated {{ generated_at }}
  </p>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">The headline</p>
  <h2>{{ headline }}</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Revenue {{ kpi.revenue.direction }} {{ kpi.revenue.delta_pct }}% against the prior
    {{ days }} days. {{ channel_top_n }} channels carry {{ channel_top_share }}% of it, and
    {{ product_top_n }} products carry {{ product_top_share }}% of product revenue.
    Concentration is the question we leave the room with.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">Where we stand today</p>
  <h2>The last {{ days }} days</h2>
  <div class="kpis">
    {% for k in kpi_cards %}
    <div class="kpi">
      <div class="label">{{ k.label }}</div>
      <div class="n">{{ k.value }}</div>
      <div class="delta {{ k.direction_class }}">{{ k.arrow }} {{ k.delta_pct }}% vs prior {{ k.basis }} days</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Every figure on these slides is queried at build time. Nothing is typed in.</p>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">Who's buying?</p>
  <h2>{{ channel_top_n }} channels do {{ channel_top_share }}% of the work.</h2>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart">{{ channel_chart }}</div>
    <div>
      <p><strong>{{ channels[0].channel }}</strong> is the largest channel at
         {{ channels[0].revenue_fmt }} ({{ channels[0].share }}% of revenue).</p>
      <p>Highest average order value: <strong>{{ channel_best_aov.channel }}</strong>
         at {{ channel_best_aov.aov_fmt }}, against a {{ kpi.aov.value }} book average.</p>
      <p class="muted"><em>Decision implication:</em> the smallest channels are where a
         percentage point costs least to buy. The largest is where it is worth most.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">What's selling?</p>
  <h2>{{ product_top_share }}% of revenue comes from {{ product_top_n }} products.</h2>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart">{{ product_chart }}</div>
    <div>
      <p>The head-and-tail pattern most retailers see.</p>
      <p>At the other end, <strong>{{ slow_count }} active products sold
         {{ slow_max_units }} units or fewer in {{ slow_window }} days</strong>. They hold
         <strong>{{ slow_capital }}</strong> of inventory at cost.</p>
      <blockquote>Every dollar tied up in a slow mover is a dollar we couldn't use to
        restock a hero SKU.</blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">Where's the margin?</p>
  <h2>Revenue and margin don't rank the same.</h2>
  <div class="chart">{{ margin_chart }}</div>
  <p>{{ margin_note }}</p>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">Where are the leaks?</p>
  <h2>{{ funnel_headline }}</h2>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart">{{ funnel_chart }}</div>
    <div>
      <p>The largest drop is <strong>{{ funnel_worst_step }}</strong>, losing
         {{ funnel_worst_loss }}% of the people who reach it.</p>
      <p>At the current basket of {{ kpi.aov.value }}, one extra percentage point through
         that step is worth about <strong>{{ funnel_point_value }}</strong> per {{ days }} days.</p>
      <p class="note">Checkout-start is excluded: seeded carts and orders are not linked,
        so that step does not reconcile against the others.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">Looking forward</p>
  <h2>What we expect, with confidence.</h2>
  <div class="chart">{{ forecast_chart }}</div>
  <p>The model projects <strong>{{ forecast_total }}</strong> over the next
     {{ forecast_days }} days, within an 80% band of
     <strong>{{ forecast_low }} to {{ forecast_high }}</strong>.</p>
  <p>Backtested over {{ metrics.n_splits }} splits it lands within
     <strong>{{ metrics.mape_pct }}%</strong> of actual on average, and its 80% band held the
     true value <strong>{{ metrics.coverage_pct }}%</strong> of the time — so the band is honest.</p>
  <p class="muted">It knows about weekly cycles, seasonality and trend. It does not know about
     promotions we haven't run, launches, or external shocks. Use the band, not the point.</p>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <p class="pill">The ask</p>
  <h2>Three commitments for next quarter.</h2>
  <table class="summary">
    <tr><th>Initiative</th><th>Why</th><th>Estimated impact</th></tr>
    {% for row in asks %}
    <tr><td>{{ row.what }}</td><td>{{ row.why }}</td><td>{{ row.impact }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <p class="source">Impacts are arithmetic on the figures above, not forecasts: one point of
     funnel movement at current AOV, and inventory valued at cost.</p>
</section>

<section class="slide title">
  <h1>Thank you.</h1>
  <p>Questions, gut-checks, sceptical pushback — all welcome.</p>
</section>

</body>
</html>
